{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqrieazbal4","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"LLM grader + enrich are the production default (ORCH_SEARCH_GRADER retired)","summary":"2026-06-23: feat/grader-provider-agnostic merged to main (merge e4081a0b) — the provider-agnostic createDefaultGraderBackend (api kind -> callApi, else spawns the active agentic-cli provider via buildInvocation/parseResult, so the grader runs on the Claude OAuth CLI with no api key) plus the code:0.16 tier de-abstain boost (fix/code-tier-gate). Then the grader was made the PRODUCTION DEFAULT (commit e059d3a6): lib/subconscious/index.js defaultSubconsciousStore now passes graderEnabled:true (routes/subconscious.js uses defaultSubconsciousStore), the ORCH_SEARCH_GRADER env flag was REMOVED, and the bare library default (createSubconsciousStore with no graderEnabled) stays OFF so unit tests never spawn a CLI. Per-request use_grader:false / grader:false opts a single call out; graderEnabled:false opts a whole store out. Enrich (code_node body fold) is also default-on (merge 052b6709). Cost: ~21s per grader call (LLM-as-arbiter latency). Daemon restarted to load it (single instance, /ping 200). Tests: 26/26 grader-module pass; subconscious integration 40 pass, 1 PRE-EXISTING Windows execution-permit allowed_paths path-separator failure (proven failing identically on pre-grader-default). Rollback: git tag pre-grader-default (052b6709). This supersedes the earlier \"grader flag-OFF by default\" state.","category":"project","tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-24T03:23:58.103Z","vec":[-0.11128199845552444,0.026458431035280228,-0.048145730048418045,-0.03333777189254761,0.030188696458935738,-0.07894445210695267,-0.09313937276601791,0.030537478625774384,-0.021414151415228844,0.011503900401294231,0.05617407709360123,-0.03292698413133621,0.017099831253290176,0.00501049030572176,0.01711718551814556,0.028189213946461678,0.047826796770095825,-0.002913320902734995,-0.06043140962719917,-0.000010912700417